A||||0||BellaFiero||On Rice and Disturbing Behavior...||||8||
Z||000000||BellaFiero||07-05-2000||12:14 PM||||<BR>I’m probably not going to make any friends with this topic… but oh well. I need to get this off my chest.<BR>I understand the Riceboys. I really do. Hell, my car could be considered rice in some circles. It probably IS considered rice. Domestic rice. Uncle Ben rice. But still – rice. I’ve got the Fi-air-O scoops from Canada over the roof, I’ve got the spoiler and the aero nose, and now I’ve added a front hood scoop ( a cobra mini-jet from A&A ). It’s all painted and clear coated and waxed – to me, it looks good. I have flexible piping running from the back of the scoop and down around the radiator, pointing at the fan. Will it actually help? Probably not – not sure yet. But it hasn’t hurt in the three days it’s been done. Yes, the scoop color-matches the car. It would be hard to tell if my car wasn’t some sport model out of Calloway or some such. But seriously – it’s a four cylinder. It is completely for show. I don’t pretend my car is a Ferrari. But it might look like one now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. I was going for the front scoop on the Marenello ( spelling? ) and I found this scoop instead… and I love it. I’ve never cared what anyone else thought. And I still don’t.<BR>But as I was driving down the main strip through Fairview, I passed a Fantasy Motorsports shop. Outside were parked an assortment of body-modded and super-spoilered vehicles. I’ve got a lot of aftermarket performance equipment on my car – mostly modified in some way to work with my little engine-in-the-back baby – and so I’m very confident of my car’s abilities against another four cylinder. Even today’s 4s. So why not… <BR>Naturally, the Boys of Rice would not let a challenge go without answer. They pulled up next to me, four young men in a bright blue Civic. It actually did look good – I’m sorry, but it did. I like the body mods. I like the tint and the lights and all that sort of thing ( except for the clear brake lights – whoever thought that up… oui… ) anyways. They started making… disparaging comments about my girlfriend, and then tsked tsked my “ancient” car.<BR>Needless to say, their faces were a wash of red as my little Bella Donna fired up ahead of them. Red light racing at it’s best, we hit red light after red light, and at each green I pulled out in front of them. Now, it wasn’t a peel of smoke and I took off like a bat out of hell until they dissapeared in my rear view mirror. But I did best them every time…<BR>… so they tried scare tactics on me. They started following me around, blasting their music and doing their best to look menacing. Crystal wanted to call the cops on the cell, but I wanted to have my fun. When I get my pictures up, any day, you’ll see that I’ve converted a lot of the interior into a custom job. I wanted my car’s inside to match the “exotic” aspect I’ve done to the outside. And being an “exotic” – you HAVE to have the talking radar detector from Cobra!! Come on, people – it’s not a sport’s car if it doesn’t have a voice-alert in there… just like Knight Rider!! So we cruised until my Cobra started in with her “Be careful… X Alert…” … and at that red light, I romped and romped on the accelerator, and the Rice Boys’s bumble bee exhaust hollered right back…<BR>… light went green, they squalled tires and took off, and I sat back and watched with delight as the cherries were popped and the police officer shot out of the Schnucks parking lot, putting us both to shame with the speed of his car as he proceeding in pulling over Sir Rice and the Boys.<BR>I guess what made me mad out of all of this was the attitude. Once they found that I was beating their car, they tried to intimidate me… scare me. Cutting me off, looking at me with the most evil of faces, giving me the finger.. etc. and so on. Now, I know that red light racing isn’t exactly professional, but you’d think they’d have the courtesy to lose without being complete jerks about it… I just don’t like the attitude behind most car’s steering wheels nowadays… <BR>||||reg||8
